{sov: Notes}
Soul Jazz Groove: Driven by a mid-tempo, boogaloo-style soul jazz feel.
The underlying harmonic structure is a standard 12-bar blues in F.

Rhythm Section: Focus heavily on the syncopated bassline and snappy snare
backbeat. Guitar and piano should keep chord stabs syncopated on the offbeats.

Voicings: Use punchy 9th or 13th dominant voicings (F9, Bb9, C9) to dial in
that authentic late-'60s Chicago soul sound.

Vamp & Solos: Solo sections blow open over the 12-bar frame or stay locked
on a static F7 vamp depending on live arrangement preferences.
{eov}